    "narrative": "The clear engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Corbin Carroll**, who registers an elite score of 80.87. He is the priority start, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Roki Sasaki; the combination of a high-upside batting order slot and the opposition's slow delivery provides a massive ceiling for stolen bases\u2014our most precious commodity. **Brice Turang** (68.83) and **Mickey Moniak** (68.23) also provide excellent value. **Brice Turang** is particularly well-positioned as a leadoff catalyst against Matthews, with the favorable SB environment boosting his floor, while **Mickey Moniak** serves as a high-upside platoon play, utilizing a significant 14% platoon edge to offset a lackluster park factor.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles, specifically regarding our lineup configuration. **Isaac Paredes** (59.92) just barely misses the \"Strong\" start threshold due to a difficult matchup against Robbie Ray, but his volume in the #3 hole keeps him firmly in the lineup. The most difficult bench decision involved **Cole Young**, who provided a 35.19 score. While his profile was considered, his expected spot at #9 against a tough arm like Drew Rasmussen relegated him to the bench in favor of higher-ceiling options like **Max Muncy** and **Austin Riley**. Note that **Josh Naylor**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Isaac Paredes** are currently listed with \"Lineup Pending\" status; if their confirmed batting orders deviate significantly from our projections, their efficiency scores\u2014and subsequent starting status\u2014could shift rapidly. Keep a close eye on these slots to ensure we aren't burning limited game caps on suboptimal lineup spots.",
